  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-Sectoral Support for Conflict-Affected Populations and Vulnerable Migrants in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2019, Lebanon has endured a complex political and economic crisis, leading to the collapse of public infrastructure and essential services and a significant increase in poverty across the country, including among Lebanon&#x2019;s 170,000 migrant workers and their families. Additionally, since the outbreak of hostilities in Gaza on 7 October 2023, cross-border clashes between Israel and Hezbollah have intensified daily. These clashes have caused significant material damage to public and private properties and led to the internal displacement of an estimated 100,000 people. Through this project, the International Organization for Migration is implementing a multi-sectoral approach to address the humanitarian needs of internally displaced persons fleeing the south and migrants in vulnerable situations, mitigating their exposure to abuse through protection services and advocacy work with employers to strengthen migrant worker protection.</narrative>
  </description>
